{Take a pawn, then convert with an e-pawn and active rooks. Kramnik took Kasparov's title
in this match. Here he grabs the b7 pawn and shows Kasparov's dynamic play wasn't enough.}
1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. cxd5 Nxd5 5. e4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 Bg7 7. Nf3 c5 8. Be3 Qa5 9.
Qd2 Bg4 10. Rb1 a6 11. Rxb7 {Grabs the pawn. The engine rates it about equal, and Kramnik
trusted his technique.} 11... Bxf3 12. gxf3 Nc6 13. Bc4 O-O 14. O-O cxd4 15. cxd4 Bxd4 16.
Bd5 Bc3 17. Qc1 Nd4 18. Bxd4 Bxd4 19. Rxe7 Ra7 20. Rxa7 Bxa7 21. f4 Qd8 22. Qc3 Bb8 23.
Qf3 Qh4 24. e5 {The e-pawn starts to roll.} 24... g5 25. Re1 Qxf4 26. Qxf4 gxf4 27. e6
{Gives the pawn to activate the rook.} 27... fxe6 28. Rxe6 Kg7 29. Rxa6 Rf5 30. Be4 Re5
31. f3 Re7 32. a4 Ra7 33. Rb6 Be5 34. Rb4 Rd7 35. Kg2 Rd2+ 36. Kh3 h5 37. Rb5 Kf6 38. a5
Ra2 39. Rb6+ Ke7 40. Bd5 {Kasparov resigned. The a-pawn decides.} 1-0
